    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the clear anchor of the Austin Waves lineup. With an elite efficiency score of 81.88, he benefits from a highly favorable park factor (+16%) and an advantageous matchup against S. Lugo, whose 4.53 xERA provides a soft landing spot for Henderson\u2019s high-ceiling profile. Joining him at the top of the production hierarchy are **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63). **Kyle Tucker** thrives despite the neutral platoon dynamic, leveraging a significant SP skill edge against Bratt, while **Jacob Wilson** is primed to exploit the 5.23 xERA of Schultz. We are also monitoring the speed-focused outings for **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill**; while their scores are bolstered by specific SP delivery patterns that inflate their stolen base probability, their situational edges against Bradley and Gausman make them essential components of our pursuit of league-leading SB totals.\n\nOur toughest roster exclusion today was **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 56.28. While his 19% SP skill advantage against Phillips was promising, he ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace our high-floor starters. Similarly, **Miguel Vargas** remains on the bench despite an elite 0.403 xwOBA; however, the defensive variables and the superior efficiency ratings of our starting middle infielders prioritized **Sam Antonacci** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** today. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Liam Hicks** (43.11), who carries the lowest score in our starting nine due to a negative park factor and a difficult dynamic platoon split against Cantillo. Keep a close watch on **Heliot Ramos** and **Andy Pages**; while both occupy favorable spots in their respective lineups, any late-breaking weather alerts in their games could necessitate an immediate pivot to our more stable bench depth.",
